# packwiz refresh hashes files as checked out locally. GitHub always serves
# committed blobs with LF line endings, so any contributor on a machine with
# core.autocrlf=true silently corrupts every text-file hash in index.toml —
# the file still reads fine, but packwiz-installer's hash check fails for
# every affected entry on every client. Force LF so local hashing always
# matches what's actually served.
* text=auto eol=lf
